<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>The Ripple Effect — Mentorship</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/tailwindcss@2.2.19/dist/tailwind.min.css">
</head>
<body class="bg-gray-100">
  <main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto my-10 p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg">
    <header class="flex gap-4 items-center flex-wrap">
      <img alt="Mentorship" src="/assets/mentorship-classroom.jpg" class="w-24 h-24 object-cover rounded-lg hidden md:block"/>
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-700">The Ripple Effect: How Mentorship Transforms a Community</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mt-1">
          Mentorship is more than guidance — it's a multiplier. One empowered student influences peers, families and local institutions, producing long-term social and economic gains.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-3 items-center text-sm text-gray-500">
          <span class="bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 px-3 py-1 rounded-full font-semibold">
            Program: Community Mentors
          </span>
          <time datetime="2025-10-07">Updated: Oct 07, 2025</time>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="grid md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px] gap-5 mt-7" id="overview">
      <div>
        <article class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl shadow-inner border border-gray-100">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Overview</h2>
          <p>
            Mentorship pairs experienced volunteers with students to build skills, confidence and social capital. Over time, mentees apply what they learn in school, at home and in community projects — creating a ripple that reaches far beyond the classroom.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">How the ripple works</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Skill gains:</strong> targeted support improves academic outcomes and practical skills.</li>
            <li><strong>Confidence & leadership:</strong> mentees take on peer-teaching and local initiatives.</li>
            <li><strong>Family uplift:</strong> improved outcomes influence siblings and parents, who invest more in education.</li>
            <li><strong>Community impact:</strong> better-educated residents strengthen local economies and civic engagement.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Measurable outcomes to track</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>Attendance and retention rates</li>
            <li>Academic performance (grades, test scores)</li>
            <li>Peer mentoring activities started by alumni</li>
            <li>Household-level changes (saving for school, reduced child labour)</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="flex gap-3 mt-4">
            <button class="bg-blue-700 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-lg font-semibold" onclick="window.print()">
              Print / Save
            </button>
            <button class="border border-blue-200 text-blue-700 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg font-semibold" onclick="document.getElementById('contact').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' })">
              Contact Program
            </button>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl shadow-inner border border-gray-100 mt-5">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Short case study</h2>
          <p>
            In one village program, students who had weekly mentoring increased school attendance by 15% within a year. Several of those students went on to lead study groups and sports activities that engaged younger children — a direct example of the ripple effect.
          </p>
          <blockquote class="italic border-l-4 border-blue-100 pl-3 mt-3 text-gray-800">
            "Mentorship gave me the confidence to start a small tutoring group — now three younger students are back in school full-time." — Amina, former mentee
          </blockquote>
        </article>
      </div>

      <aside class="space-y-5">
        <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl shadow-inner border border-gray-100">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Ways to get involved</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>Volunteer as a mentor (1–3 hours/week)</li>
            <li>Support materials & supplies</li>
            <li>Host a skills workshop (computing, entrepreneurship)</li>
            <li>Sponsor transport or uniforms for mentees</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Quick facts</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>Mentor commitment: flexible</li>
            <li>Age range: 13–24 (mentees)</li>
            <li>Typical group size: 8–15 students</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl shadow-inner border border-gray-100">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Get program resources</h2>
          <p>Download our brief toolkit for starting a mentorship circle.</p>
          <div class="flex gap-3 mt-3">
            <a href="/resources/mentorship-toolkit.pdf" download class="bg-blue-700 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-lg font-semibold">
              Download PDF
            </a>
            <a href="#contact" class="border border-blue-200 text-blue-700 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg font-semibold">
              Request support
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <footer id="contact" class="mt-8 pt-5 border-t border-gray-100 flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
      <div>
        <strong>Contact the Mentorship Team</strong>
        <div class="mt-1">
          Email: <a href="mailto:mentors@example.org" class="text-blue-700">mentors@example.org</a> — Phone: +254 700 000 000
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-right">
        <div>Share this page:</div>
        <div class="mt-2 flex gap-2 justify-end">
          <button class="border border-blue-200 text-blue-700 px-3 py-1 rounded-lg" onclick="if (navigator.share) { navigator.share({ title: document.title, url: window.location.href }); } else { alert('Sharing not supported'); }">
            Share
          </button>
          <button class="bg-blue-700 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-lg" onclick="history.back()">
            Back
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>
</body>
</html>